      "dcDescription": [
        "Morral is the native name for the square wool shoulder bags, as worn and knitted by men. This morral is knitted from dark brown and white wool. The square part is knitted in one piece, after which it is folded and closed at the sides. The front and back are identical: within a decorative border of zigzag lines and square blocks, a galloping horse is depicted, with two suns at the top right and bottom left. The handle consists of two parts, which are attached to the side of the bag. The long handle part is tied to the short one to the desired height.This morral was made by Manuel and bought at "
